STATUS
Exact bounded diagnostics for Target 5A8H28R13.  The identity count
compares the last-exit Green channel sum with an independent endpoint
recurrence.  The outside-in signs are bounded discovery evidence only;
Lemma 5A8H28UC, not the scan, proves the channel decomposition.  The
renewal-current signs test and refute the stronger coefficientwise
shortcut P_(n,t)(F-1)>=0.  The same run verifies the exact
two-vertex Green-minor and divided-core identities and refutes both
independent-factor positivity shortcuts in P5A.102CB5P.  It also
tests the three interval pieces in P5A.102CB5U and the strict deficit
reserve P5A.102CB5V.  The local-triple and nested-radius counters are
negative controls for two stronger one-dimensional allocations.  The
t=4 counters test the fixed three-step kernel, the fully smoothed
vector V_j, its first induction difference, the nine base Newton
differences W_r, and the exact vanishing of the ninth difference.
They also test the four reduced sign blocks in P5A.102CB8F and two
strictly stronger false decompositions.

