INTERPRETATION
All 200,970 last-exit channel decompositions reproduce the independent
full-prefix current exactly.  Individual-channel localization is false,
as shown by the displayed nonspecial negative and 119,127 negative
channels overall.  Nevertheless every one of the 6,116,187 cumulative
channel sums, ordered from largest |y-(K-Q)| inward, is nonnegative.
This isolates the unproved statement as the outside-in Green payment
(P5A.102CB8).  The displayed negative renewal coefficient separately
rules out coefficientwise positivity before convolution with the killed
Green channels.  All 17,110 two-vertex Green-minor identities and all
26,477 divided-core reconstructions hold exactly.  The displayed
negative twice-return kernel and divided cores show that neither factor
in P5A.102CB5P is independently nonnegative, including when Q>=2.
The 4,269,923 higher-Q negative odd-boundary coefficients refute the
scalar separation of the reflected-pair identity P5A.102CB5X.
The interval-piece negatives show that neither upper interval is a
separate positive channel, and 94 strict rows have both upper deficits
at once.  Nevertheless all 5,915,217 strict lower-reservoir payments
P5A.102CB5V are nonnegative.  The 62,055 negative local triples and
404 negative nested-radius prefixes refute both natural
one-dimensional refinements.  These counts remain bounded evidence.
The fixed three-step t=4 kernel has 127,619 negative coordinates,
including 126,498 at Q>=2, so it cannot prove the target.  After the
required growing smoothing, all 764,295 tested V_j coordinates, all
727,900 first induction differences, and all 327,555 tested base
Newton differences W_r are nonnegative.  The ninth operator difference
vanishes identically on the tested vectors.  These t=4 sign counts are
also bounded evidence, not a proof of P5A.102CB8C.
All 36,395 tested C_4 coordinates and all 109,185 tested coordinates
of G_0,G_1,G_2 are nonnegative.  In contrast, the isolated low C_4
component has 8,304 negatives, and the order-one group without its
C_2 credit has 4,105 negatives.  Thus the four-block reduction keeps
credits that its two displayed negative controls show are necessary.
The zero counts remain bounded evidence for P5A.102CB8F.

